            <div xml:id="d815">

                <pb facs="0825" n="713" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg713"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/5285: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commissioner at Helsingfors</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Haynes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Helsingfors</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-26T23:00:00+01:39"><hi rendition="#italic">September 26,
                                1919, 11 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received September 27, 9:08
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>435. It is certain Esthonia and Latvia will conclude peace with the Bolsheviki.
                    Lithuania and Finland unlikely but Finland may if the Socialists succeed in
                    their efforts to have Diet called to decide the matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Haynes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
